.idea/

# android/ is untracked entirely (Expo CNG regenerates it from app.json),
# but if it's ever committed, none of these should go with it: they all
# bake in machine-specific absolute paths (a Windows "C:\dev\..." path on
# this machine breaks a Linux EAS builder, and vice versa), and the .cxx/
# CMake caches and hs_err_pid crash dumps are pure local-build noise.
android/.cxx/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/app/.cxx/
android/local.properties
**/android/.cxx/
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# EAS Build archives and uploads the local project directory as-is (it
# does not clone a clean checkout from GitHub for this command) --
# .gitignore alone does not control what goes into that archive. This
# locally-generated native project (with this machine's absolute paths
# baked into local.properties, .cxx caches, etc.) must never be part of
# the upload: EAS must always perform its own clean Linux prebuild from
# app.json, the same way it did for the versionCode 24 build that
# succeeded before this android/ directory existed locally.
/android
/ios
